{"schema_version":"1","crate":"adacl_aunit","version":"8.0.0","id":"7947bdb8ffdc2d10","name":"AdaCL.Command_Line.GetOpt","qualified_name":"AdaCL.Command_Line.GetOpt","kind":"ada_package","location":{"file":"../../../home/runner/.local/share/alire/builds/adacl_desktop_8.0.0_f8165a62/7c9a0f33cae7856c47501686ef2314b0824249fe5ea51ba4b7d3b9d056e57426/src/adacl-command_line-getopt.ads","line":53,"column":9},"code":"package AdaCL.Command_Line.GetOpt","documentation":{"description":"-\n  @summary\n  Object-oriented GNU GetOpt command-line parser.\n\n  @description\n  Parse short options, GNU long options, and positional file names from Ada.Command_Line. The scanner is a tagged\n  type: every piece of parser state lives in the instance, so two tasks may parse the command line independently.\n\n  Derive from Object, set the POSIX option pattern in an overriding Parse, and handle tokens in\n  Analyze_Without_Argument, Analyze_With_Argument, Analyze_GNU, and Analyze_File. Write_Help is called when\n  the built-in help option is seen.\n\n  Option letters, long names, and file names are Wide_Wide_String values, so they may contain characters outside\n  Latin-1.\n\n  The child name GetOpt is an intentional exception to Ada underscore style. It is the POSIX / GNU proper name of\n  this interface; GNAT uses the same token for GNAT.Command_Line.Getopt. New identifiers inside this package use\n  underscored Ada names."},"simple_types":[{"id":"ecaa392c9b97a415","name":"Found_Flag","qualified_name":"AdaCL.Command_Line.GetOpt.Found_Flag","kind":"ada_simple_type","location":{"file":"../../../home/runner/.local/share/alire/builds/adacl_desktop_8.0.0_f8165a62/7c9a0f33cae7856c47501686ef2314b0824249fe5ea51ba4b7d3b9d056e57426/src/adacl-command_line-getopt.ads","line":73,"column":9},"code":"type Found_Flag is\n   (End_Of_Options,\n    No_Option,\n    GNU_Style,\n    With_Argument,\n    Without_Argument,\n    Error);"}],"tagged_types":[{"id":"a6224027e4e2a2e3","name":"Object","qualified_name":"A